Track 2: Who Severed the Scion?
- Story & Context: Huddled beneath the sodium heat lamps of Ceres Greenhouse as condensation beaded against the iron frames, Tariq Finch confronted his own stylistic vanity after Noah Yunupingu accused him of using the yidaki as cheap retro decoration for quick clever rhymes. Noah walked out into the rain, abandoning his eucalyptus log propped humming against an electric space heater whose copper elements hissed against the damp peat moss. Staring at the shredded magnetic ribbon taped to the glass wall like a botanical specimen, Tariq realized the time-capsule tape had degraded specifically where the circular breath met the Rhodes chords, writing his most vulnerable verse straight into the room's ambient mic: "measuring my pedigree in borrowed bread, I was trimming the shoots while the taproot bled." When Noah returned at dawn smelling of wet eucalyptus leaves, he picked up the pipe without a word and harmonized beneath Tariq's confession.
