Track 3: Azimuth of the Glasshouse
- Story & Context: By the summer of 2024, word of the time-capsule tape had spread into folklore, culminating in an unauthorized daylight gathering inside the Heidelberg quarry greenhouse where Uncle Gary presided over two thousand listeners sitting shoulder-to-shoulder on sacks of potting soil. Golden dust motes swirled through cracked skylights while the dry crack of bursting wattle seed pods punctuated Noah’s circular breathing, which rattled the glass louvers like subterranean thunder. When an unexpected voltage surge from the solar array melted the capsule's cassette shell directly into the deck's playback heads, the band didn't stop, letting the molten hiss loop indefinitely under Tariq's triumphant chant: "lay the green scion in the ancient ground, the graft took hold before the sun came down." Legend holds that the cassette recorder remains entombed in hardened resin at the quarry, still vibrating faintly at 42 Hertz whenever the afternoon temperature peaks.
